3. Why this shape, not a different one
------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Reused prevent_self_verification()'s exact pattern instead of
  inventing a new mechanism, because this codebase has already solved
  "RLS can't restrict columns" once, in the same table, for a
  near-identical reason — a second, differently-shaped fix for the same
  problem would just be inconsistent for no benefit.
- Whitelisted at the signup function rather than trying to tighten
  profiles_role_check further, because the check constraint's job is
  "what values can this column ever legally hold" (still true — admins
  do need role = 'admin' to exist as a value, just never via signup),
  not "what can an unauthenticated signup request choose."
- Did not touch is_admin(), the SELECT/INSERT policies on profiles, or
  any other table — the finding's four numbered required-fix items map
  1:1 onto the trigger, the whitelist, "never trust admin from
  metadata," and "promotion via a secure server/admin path" (already
  true and left alone); item 5 (pgTAP tests) is the new test file.

